ALGORITHM: BEST TIME TO BE ALIVE

Step 1: Start.

Step 2: Read the number of scientists n.

Step 3: Read the birth year and death year of each scientist.

Step 4: Store every birth event as (+1)
        and every death event as (-1).

Step 5: Sort all events by year.
        If birth and death occur in the same year,
        process death before birth.

Step 6: Set count = 0 and max = 0.

Step 7: Process each event one by one:

        If it is a death:
            count = count - 1

        If it is a birth:
            count = count + 1

        If count > max:
            max = count
            bestYear = current year

Step 8: Display bestYear and max.

Step 9: Stop.






TIME COMPLEXITY:

Sorting birth[] array:
    O(n²)
Sorting death[] array:
    O(n²)
Processing the arrays:
    O(n)

Therefore:
Total Time Complexity
= O(n²) + O(n²) + O(n)
= O(n²)

Space Complexity:
= O(n)
